# Spirit of the Labyrinth: "Each player can't draw more than one card each turn." It applies to each card draw (CR 121.2b):
# "if you haven't drawn any cards in a turn, and a spell or ability would cause you to draw multiple cards, you'll just draw
# one card" (its ruling), and its controller is one of the players. Bot1 casts it on turn 1, then Ancestral Recall on
# itself: one card of the three. On turn 2 Bot2 draws its card for the turn, and its own Ancestral Recall draws it nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Spirit of the Labyrinth
Ancestral Recall
Forest
Plains
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Ancestral Recall
Swamp x5
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spirit of the Labyrinth.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Hand = Forest; Plains; Island
? Bot2.Hand.Count = 8
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot2)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
Bot1.Library.Count = 19
Bot2.Hand.Count = 6
Bot2.Library.Count = 19
